(FLW-45 (undocumented precision - see Discrepancy 2): `Increment` and
 `Decrement` are number-only, and the two ways they say so disagree. On a
 `float` they are a SILENT NO-OP - no diagnostic, no change. On a `text`
 the compiler refuses the program with "Increment requires a number
 variable: label". This probe carries the float half, which compiles; the
 text half is D2.vox.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox FLW-45.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   2.25
   2.25
   2.25
)
